WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Proficiency.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:08.386
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.686 --> 00:00:17.016
Unit twenty: The Future of Education. In this unit, you will discuss how education will change and adapt style to different audiences.

4
00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:20.005
lifelong learning society.

5
00:00:20.705 --> 00:00:26.919
lifelong learning society means a society where people keep learning throughout their lives.

6
00:00:27.219 --> 00:00:31.575
A lifelong learning society needs flexible courses.

7
00:00:32.275 --> 00:00:36.413
Your turn. Say: lifelong learning society.

8
00:00:39.113 --> 00:00:40.892
lifelong learning society.

9
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:43.593
credential inflation.

10
00:00:44.293 --> 00:00:49.694
credential inflation means needing ever higher qualifications for the same jobs.

11
00:00:49.994 --> 00:00:52.864
Credential inflation makes degrees less valuable.

12
00:00:53.564 --> 00:00:56.994
Your turn. Say: credential inflation.

13
00:00:59.694 --> 00:01:01.253
credential inflation.

14
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.623
micro-credential.

15
00:01:04.323 --> 00:01:09.050
micro-credential means a short certificate proving a specific skill.

16
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:13.266
She earned a micro-credential in data analysis.

17
00:01:13.966 --> 00:01:17.651
Your turn. Say: micro-credential.

18
00:01:20.351 --> 00:01:21.782
micro-credential.

19
00:01:22.783 --> 00:01:24.226
personalised learning.

20
00:01:24.926 --> 00:01:29.967
personalised learning means teaching adapted to each learner's needs and pace.

21
00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:33.369
Personalised learning helps weaker students catch up.

22
00:01:34.069 --> 00:01:37.442
Your turn. Say: personalised learning.

23
00:01:40.142 --> 00:01:41.607
personalised learning.

24
00:01:42.617 --> 00:01:44.732
AI tutor.

25
00:01:45.432 --> 00:01:50.450
AI tutor means an artificial intelligence that helps students learn.

26
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.433
An AI tutor can explain maths at any hour.

27
00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:58.749
Your turn. Say: AI tutor.

28
00:02:01.449 --> 00:02:03.170
AI tutor.

29
00:02:04.183 --> 00:02:06.102
educational technology.

30
00:02:06.802 --> 00:02:11.773
educational technology means digital tools used for teaching and learning.

31
00:02:12.073 --> 00:02:16.209
Educational technology expanded during the pandemic.

32
00:02:16.909 --> 00:02:20.862
Your turn. Say: educational technology.

33
00:02:23.562 --> 00:02:25.445
educational technology.

34
00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.194
learning analytics.

35
00:02:28.894 --> 00:02:33.831
learning analytics means using data to understand and improve learning.

36
00:02:34.131 --> 00:02:38.186
Learning analytics show which lessons students find hard.

37
00:02:38.886 --> 00:02:42.246
Your turn. Say: learning analytics.

38
00:02:44.946 --> 00:02:46.330
learning analytics.

39
00:02:47.317 --> 00:02:48.829
knowledge society.

40
00:02:49.529 --> 00:02:54.500
knowledge society means a society in which knowledge is the main source of value.

41
00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.740
A knowledge society depends on education.

42
00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.661
Your turn. Say: knowledge society.

43
00:03:04.361 --> 00:03:05.804
knowledge society.

44
00:03:06.817 --> 00:03:09.106
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:03:09.406 --> 00:03:14.843
Ms. Sarah, how would you explain AI tutors to a parent in my village?

46
00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:21.705
Simply: 'It's like a patient helper on the phone that explains homework any time.'

47
00:03:23.017 --> 00:03:25.423
And to university administrators?

48
00:03:26.717 --> 00:03:34.001
'AI tutors enable scalable personalised learning, supported by learning analytics.'

49
00:03:35.317 --> 00:03:37.804
Same idea, very different style!

50
00:03:39.117 --> 00:03:43.661
Exactly. Style shifting means choosing words for your audience.

51
00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:47.054
What about credential inflation?

52
00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:58.377
For students I'd say: 'Degrees alone aren't enough any more.' For policymakers: 'Qualification requirements are escalating disproportionately.'

53
00:03:59.683 --> 00:04:03.808
Grammar focus: Style shifting and audience.

54
00:04:04.108 --> 00:04:07.674
C2 mastery means adapting your style to each audience.

55
00:04:07.974 --> 00:04:17.221
To a parent: it's like a patient helper that explains homework. To administrators: AI tutors enable scalable personalised learning.

56
00:04:17.521 --> 00:04:20.868
The message stays the same; the style changes.

57
00:04:21.168 --> 00:04:27.660
True C2 mastery is not always sounding formal; it is choosing the right style for each audience.

58
00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:32.835
Now read and listen. Learning in the Twenty-First Century.

59
00:04:33.135 --> 00:04:37.956
In a knowledge society, education no longer ends with a single degree.

60
00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:44.117
A lifelong learning society requires opportunities to study at every age.

61
00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:50.400
Micro-credentials allow workers to prove specific skills without years of study.

62
00:04:51.683 --> 00:04:57.886
Meanwhile, credential inflation means employers often demand higher qualifications for the same jobs.

63
00:04:59.183 --> 00:05:05.548
Educational technology, including AI tutors, promises personalised learning at scale.

64
00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:11.694
Learning analytics can help teachers identify which students need support.

65
00:05:12.983 --> 00:05:19.209
Critics warn, however, that technology cannot replace human relationships in education.

66
00:05:20.517 --> 00:05:26.626
The future of learning may depend on combining digital tools with the irreplaceable role of good teachers.

67
00:05:27.917 --> 00:05:30.650
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:34.529
Needing higher qualifications for the same jobs is blank.

69
00:05:34.829 --> 00:05:40.433
A, credential inflation. B, micro-credential. C, learning analytics.

70
00:05:44.417 --> 00:05:47.589
The answer is A: credential inflation.

71
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:51.350
Which version suits a young child?

72
00:05:51.650 --> 00:06:02.827
A, The device facilitates individualised instruction.. B, The app helps you learn at your own speed.. C, Pedagogical optimisation is achieved..

73
00:06:06.817 --> 00:06:11.173
The answer is B: The app helps you learn at your own speed..

74
00:06:12.683 --> 00:06:15.240
Which version suits an academic report?

75
00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:22.351
A, It's really useful.. B, It enables scalable personalised learning.. C, It's cool..

76
00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:30.288
The answer is B: It enables scalable personalised learning..

77
00:06:31.783 --> 00:06:35.699
A short certificate proving a specific skill is a blank.

78
00:06:35.999 --> 00:06:41.324
A, micro-credential. B, AI tutor. C, knowledge society.

79
00:06:45.317 --> 00:06:48.222
The answer is A: micro-credential.

80
00:06:49.717 --> 00:06:53.527
According to the text, what cannot technology replace?

81
00:06:53.827 --> 00:06:59.768
A, data. B, human relationships in education. C, exams.

82
00:07:03.783 --> 00:07:08.604
The answer is B: human relationships in education.

83
00:07:10.117 --> 00:07:17.436
Now it's your turn. Part one: Explain the idea of lifelong learning to two different audiences.

84
00:07:22.736 --> 00:07:27.371
Part two: Give one version for a teenager and one for a government official.

85
00:07:33.671 --> 00:07:47.019
For a teenager: 'You'll keep learning new skills your whole life, not just at school.' For an official: 'A lifelong learning system enables continuous upskilling, which strengthens productivity and social mobility.'

86
00:07:47.319 --> 00:07:49.330
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:50.317 --> 00:07:55.291
Great work today! You learned eight new words and style shifting and audience.

88
00:07:55.591 --> 00:07:59.532
Today's value is pride in learning. Be proud of what you learned.

89
00:07:59.832 --> 00:08:03.402
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

90
00:08:03.702 --> 00:08:06.598
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

